  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PatDisc_3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "During a conversation with your care team, you learn that patients are
    sometimes invited to share their perspectives early in the research process.
    This helps researchers better understand what matters most in daily life with
    a disease and design studies that reflect those needs. You respond, \u201CSo,
    by including patient voices early, new treatments are more likely to be safer
    and more effective for more people?\u201D\nIs this True or False?"
  explanation: When patients, particularly those from historically underrepresented
    groups, share their experiences, researchers can design studies that better reflect
    real-world needs. While it is not guaranteed that every new treatment will ever
    work for every patient, diverse patient perspectives increase the chances that
    discoveries will lead to safer, more effective treatments that benefit as many
    people as possible.
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Patient
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
